ngs remain consistently above or below the expected range after applying the 7–8 cm depth\" (not in Gage's sources); +1.\n\n**Observation:**  \nThe reference text states that the recommended irrigation depth per application for sugarcane is **7–8 cm**.\n\n**Analysis:**  \nApplying water to a depth of 7–8 cm per irrigation aligns with the agronomic guidelines for meeting the crop’s water demand while avoiding excess or deficit.\n\n**Confidence:**  \nHigh – the depth is explicitly given in the agricultural knowledge source.\n\n**Recommendations:**  \n\n- **Immediate actions:**  \n  - Apply irrigation water so that the infiltrated depth is between **7 cm and 8 cm** for each irrigation event.\n\n- **Monitoring advice:**  \n  - After irrigation, check soil‑moisture sensors or manually probe the soil to confirm that the moisture profile corresponds to the applied depth.  \n  - Observe the crop for any signs of water stress (wilting) or waterlogging (yellowing, root rot) and adjust future applications accordingly.\n\n- **When to seek expert help:**  \n  - If soil‑moisture readings remain consistently above or below the expected range after applying the 7–8 cm depth.  \n  - If you encounter unusual weather patterns, water‑availability constraints, or suspect irrigation system inefficiencies that prevent achieving the target depth.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 1.27, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "summary", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 202, "completion_tokens": 189, "seconds": 1.44, "status": "ok", "seq": 1}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 468, "completion_tokens": 173, "seconds": 0.7, "status": "ok", "seq": 2}, {"purpose": "answer", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 1400, "completion_tokens": 498, "seconds": 1.89, "status": "ok", "seq": 3}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 950, "completion_tokens": 565, "seconds": 1.27, "status": "ok", "seq"